name: test-lowering (braced-operand update)
prereqs: [none — extends the existing operand() reader; no new nodes]
invariant: `${name}` and `$name` are the same read, so the shared
  string-shape operand reader accepts the braced spelling exactly like
  numeric_operand always has. The braces are stripped, then the SAME
  plain-identifier gate applies, so `${v:0:1}`, `${#v}`, `${v:-x}` and
  positional `$3` still refuse (pinned by the existing
  non_affix_and_complex_operands_refuse test and two new refusal
  assertions). Three arms consume operand() and all three benefit:
  nonempty (-n/-z), glob-affix (lhs + pattern), string-eq (lhs; the
  arm's own `{`/`}` metachar guard still refuses a braced operand in
  the ==/=/!= shapes — the guard runs before operand(), so that class
  stays on the runtime path unchanged, pinned by a new test). The
  status-liveness guard is untouched: `[ -n "${VAR}" ] || VAR=x` keeps
  its test call because the || chain reads the exit status (measured:
  2 of the 10 candidate corpus sites correctly stay).
scope: offered to all (estree, c, go, java, perl, python, rust, sh,
  fish, zig, zsh) — the lift is target-independent shIR→shIR inside
  the existing shared transform; every backend already renders the
  resulting BinOp/strHasPrefix leaves natively.
updates: test-lowering (accepted canonical set, transforms.rs
  ("test-lowering", test_lowering::transform) — registration unchanged;
  this offer is the delta in operand() plus the
  braced_var_operands_lower_like_plain_ones unit test).
metrics: sh2 callouts TOTAL 2302 → 2294 (test 166 → 158), measured
  with plmetric over the 560-example corpus. 8 of 10 candidate sites
  lift: the -n "${so}"/-n "${se}" pairs in id-cmdsub/readonly-cmdsub/
  tty-cmdsub, -n "${iface}" (dqs-nested-awk-sed), -z
  "${INTERPRETER_UNDER_TEST}" (heredoc-binary-data), and one more -n
  site; the 2 func-after-* sites stay (status liveness — refuse >
  guess). Corpus-wide shIR byte-diff vs the pre-offer binary: exactly
  5 files changed (dqs-nested-awk-sed, heredoc-binary-data, id-cmdsub,
  readonly-cmdsub, tty-cmdsub); the other 555 examples are
  byte-identical.
gates (2026-10-20, this workspace): sh2perl lib 1391 pass / 10 fail —
  the 10 are the pre-existing c_backend baseline (failure set diffed
  identical with and without the change); test_lowering module 14/14
  green (13 existing + 1 new); check_qx green on all 7 touched
